<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korea says finds unfair stock trading.</title>
<headline>South Korea says finds unfair stock trading.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Securities Supervisory Board (SSB) said on Friday it had found unfair stock trading by 17 dealers and company executives.</p>
<p>It said the unfair trading involved shares of seven companies, including Keum Kang Leather.  </p>
<p>The board said it had reported 10 company officials, including a major shareholder of Keum Kang and an excutive of Hyundai Paint, to state prosecutors for insider trading.</p>
<p>Others, mostly brokers, were accused of manipulating stock prices and using false names in share trading.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
